Melodee v1.6.0-rc.7 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/keremimo/melodee tag v1.6.0-rc.7
(commit 022bab7294d523fe0b4f48581c8afecc39fc4446; source: https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/archive/022bab7294d523fe0b4f48581c8afecc39fc4446.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. Copyright (C) 2026 Kerem Kilic (Ellic Studio); portions Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita, Hügelton Instruments (Felucca).
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/melodee_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as Melodee's own host tests do (tests/hostsim.c, ui_test.c, backup_test.c, editor_test.c)
and replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx in/out through usb.c's rings), CPU1 jobs run serially,
no BLE, no USB host, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only), no overload shedding. Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/keremimo/melodee at commit 022bab7294d523fe0b4f48581c8afecc39fc4446
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, the glue tools/studio/melodee_studio.c and the shim tools/wasm_shim. A tarball of exactly this commit
(melodee-022bab7294d523fe0b4f48581c8afecc39fc4446.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
Written offer: for at least three years after the last release that ships this build, the maintainers of
FM-1 Companion will give anyone a copy of that corresponding source on request (https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/issues),
free of charge apart from the cost of physically performing the distribution.
